# Local workspace state. The glob covers every variant -- `.codeatlas/`,
# `.codeatlas-sa/` (standalone) and the ad-hoc `-audit` / `-browsercheck`
# dirs. Previously only `.codeatlas/` was listed, which left the standalone's
# state.db publishable; these stores hold indexed content from whatever
# workspace was open.
.codeatlas/
.codeatlas*/
webview-ui/dist/
webview-ui/node_modules/
.DS_Store
e2e/screenshots/
e2e/e2e/screenshots/
e2e/test-results/
test-results/
e2e/real-repos/
.tsbuildinfo
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
mcp-package/dist/
mcp-package/node_modules/
mcp-package/*.tgz
.live-verify-snapshots/
.npmrc
mcp-package/.npmrc
e2e/benchmark/llm.config.json
e2e/benchmark/results/

# ─── Not for the public repository ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Internal engineering material: ADRs, specs, defect history, agent config.
# Excluded so an orphan-branch `git add -A` cannot carry them into the public
# remote by accident.
#
# IMPORTANT: .gitignore does NOT apply to files git already tracks. All of the
# paths below ARE tracked today (docs/ alone is 120 files). On the orphan
# branch you must empty the index first or they will be committed anyway:
#
#     git checkout --orphan public/main
#     git rm -r --cached .        # <-- without this, the entries below do nothing
#     git add -A
#     git status                  # confirm before committing
#
# Trade-off to be aware of: once these are ignored, the private repo stops
# tracking changes to them too. The existing history keeps every past version,
# but new edits to docs/ and the files below will be untracked going forward.

docs/
ISSUES.md
ACTION-PLAN.md
ACTION-PLAN-*.md
prd.md
UX-FINDINGS-*.md
LIVE-VERIFY-*.md
NOTES-*.md
findings-*.md
verify-*.md

# Agent configuration and project instructions. CLAUDE.md documents internal
# verification workflow, known-flaky tests and pre-existing lint errors. If you
# would rather give contributors the architecture notes it contains, remove
# this line and review the file for internal-only detail first.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
